# World binaries go through Git LFS. Each Marble world is a large file and she
# only gets one a day, so they must not bloat the git history.
#
# IMPORTANT: run `npm run lfs:setup` once, BEFORE pushing, to install and enable
# LFS. Until git-lfs is installed these patterns do nothing and files are stored
# as ordinary blobs (git does not error) — `git lfs migrate import` converts any
# that were committed early.
#
# .ply is deliberately NOT tracked: the only .ply is the small practice world,
# and it must stay a plain blob so the four games are playable even somewhere
# git-lfs is missing. Marble's real worlds are .spz and do go through LFS.
worlds/**/*.spz  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
worlds/**/*.glb  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
docs/worlds/**/*.spz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Keep line endings sane for everything else.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.wav  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.png  binary
